spes graphics: accept client-memory IOSurfaces with an unpadded last row (0191).

CoreAnimation in backboardd wraps its own pixels and sizes them with an unpadded last row:
1105x1160 BGRA at 4448 bytes a row with IOSurfaceAllocSize 4448*1159 + 1105*4 = 5159652, and
256x1 at 672 bytes a row with 512 (0190 log, 2026-11-17). sweet_surface_layout required
bytesPerRow * rows and refused about 1000 creates a boot with kIOReturnBadArgument. For single-plane
surfaces around client memory the required extent is now offset + bytesPerRow * (rows - 1) + the last
row's pixels; the surface keeps the client's exact size. The kernel's own readers stay inside it:
SweetFramebuffer computes the last byte exactly and checks the scanout window against the memory
length (such a surface is copied, not scanned out).

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
index fefc857..69aed6d 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
@@ -557,7 +557,19 @@ sweet_surface_layout(SweetSurface *s, OSDictionary *props)
 	/* Client-owned pictures must keep their exact extent (HackiOS MiniIOSurface). */
 	if (props->getObject("IOSurfaceAddress") != NULL) {
 		uint64_t supplied = sweet_dict_u32(props, "IOSurfaceAllocSize", (uint32_t)end);
-		if (supplied < end) return kIOReturnBadArgument;
+		/*
+		 * 0191: CoreAnimation wraps its own pixels with an unpadded last row: 1105x1160 BGRA at
+		 * 4448 bytes a row comes with IOSurfaceAllocSize 4448*1159 + 1105*4 = 5159652, 256x1 at
+		 * 672 with 512 (0190 log). Requiring bytesPerRow * rows refused about 1000 of backboardd's
+		 * creates a boot. For single-plane client memory the last row only needs its pixels.
+		 */
+		uint64_t need = end;
+		uint32_t rows = sweet_div_up(s->height, s->elementHeight);
+		if (s->planeCount == 0 && rows > 0) {
+			need = (uint64_t)s->offset + (uint64_t)s->bytesPerRow * (rows - 1) +
+			    (uint64_t)sweet_div_up(s->width, s->elementWidth) * s->bytesPerElement;
+		}
+		if (supplied < need) return kIOReturnBadArgument;
 		alloc = supplied;
 	} else {
 		alloc = round_page(alloc);
